exports[`the messages > a fresh action 1`] = `
[
  {
    "content": "# The world as it stands

This is regenerated every turn and is always current. Turn 1.

## The player character

**Testy** — level 1, referred to in diffs as \`player\`.
Hit points **15/15**.
STR +3 (defense 13) · DEX +3 (defense 13) · CON +3 (defense 13) · INT +3 (defense 13) · WIS +3 (defense 13) · CHA +3 (defense 13)
Armour defense 15 · melee attack +3 · ranged attack +3
Inventory slots 10/13
Conditions: none

Carrying:
- [test-sword] Sword — 2 slots, quality 3/3
- [test-chain] Chain — 3 slots, quality 5/5
- [test-spellbook] Spellbook: Telekinesis — 1 slot
- [test-helmet] Helmet — 1 slot, quality 1/1
- [test-rations] Travel Rations — 1 slot
- [test-lantern] Lantern — 1 slot
- [test-rope] Rope — 1 slot

Equipped — weapon: [test-sword] Sword · armor: [test-chain] Chain · helmet: [test-helmet] Helmet · shield: —

Traits: physique Wiry, face Bony, skin Ashen, hair Cropped, clothing Patched, virtue Cautious, vice Greedy, speech Blunt, background Burglar, misfortunes Exiled, alignment Neutrality

## The room the player is standing in

[«id-1»] **The Cavern** (NEVER ENCOUNTERED)
base: A cavern of the drowned mint, its walls pale limestone crusted with mineral scale. Water lies ankle-deep across the floor, still and cold. Nothing has disturbed it in a long time.

### As drawn on the map
a small chamber, about 10 by 35 feet -- long and narrow, running north-south, close to a rectangle, give or take a corner. Ways out: one off the north wall, one off the east wall
The compass here is the MAP's, not the party's: north is north wherever they are facing. Say "the north wall"; never "on your left", which you have no way to know.

### In it
- [«id-2»] the rubble — RoomFeature · near the way in (NEVER ENCOUNTERED)
    base: The rubble of the drowned mint, scaled with mineral crust.
- [«id-3»] the pillars — RoomFeature · spread through the room (NEVER ENCOUNTERED)
    base: The pillars of the drowned mint, scaled with mineral crust.

### Ways out
- [«id-4»] "the mint's stair — out of the dungeon" — A broad flight of worn limestone steps rising out of the water toward the surface. · in the east wall, toward the south end · LEADS OUT OF THE DUNGEON — the way they came in, and the way home. Walking through it ENDS THE RUN: commit nextStage "departed"
- [«id-5»] "a low arch" — a low arch of fitted stone, its keystone dropped an inch · in the north wall, at the middle · leads to [«id-6»], somewhere they have not been
",
    "role": "user",
  },
  {
    "content": "The player says: I look at the far wall",
    "role": "user",
  },
  {
    "content": "# The player has acted

Their words are the last message above. Resume the heuristic at the step you were given and carry it as far as it goes.

Work through the heuristic in the open — none of it is shown to the player. Put the words they read inside \`<post>\` tags, once, at the end. Then end your turn with a single \`commit_state\` call. Every number you use must have come from the \`roll\` tool or from the player's own roll above.",
    "role": "user",
  },
]
`;

